 "notes": [
  "2018 (2018 Registration Document p.237-244): figures as originally reported, BEFORE IFRS 16. The 2019 URD restated 2018 under IFRS 16 (full retrospective): e.g. ROI 2,075.3 (vs 2,045.0), net income 1,405.5 (vs 1,404.6), total assets 8,451.9 (vs 7,468.1); restated values NOT used here.",
  "2018 non-recurring item: +52.7 = net gain on disposal of the former Galleria store premises in Hong Kong (Note 7, p.258); gain was non-taxable, lowering the 2018 tax rate by 0.8pt. Held in Asia-Pacific (excl. Japan) segment.",
  "2018 cash flow statement shows 'Depreciation and amortisation' (217.0, PP&E/intangibles/investment property) and 'Impairment losses' (43.0) on separate lines; cf.da/memo.da_cf = 217.0 excludes impairment. Note 6 'Amortisation' line within Other income and expenses = 181.5 (rest of the 217.0 is in cost of sales).",
  "2018 cash flow statement has no single 'Operating investments' line: Acquisitions of intangible assets (62.2) and of PP&E (250.1) shown separately; cf.capex = -312.3 taken from the 'Operating investments' line of the FCF reconciliation (2018 RD section 4.2, p.229).",
  "2018 apm.adj_fcf = 'Free cash flow' 1,447.3 (old definition: operating cash flows + change in WCR - operating investments; pre-IFRS 16, no lease repayment). 2019 URD shows 2018 restated adjusted FCF of 1,447.1.",
  "2018 apm.cash_inv_gt3m not printed in the 2018 document (restated net cash 3,615.1 vs net cash 3,465.1); the 2019 URD Note 3 gives 149.9 for 2018.",
  "2018 dps_exceptional = 5.00: extraordinary dividend in respect of FY2017, paid in June 2018 (together with the FY2017 ordinary dividend of 4.10). dps 4.55 = ordinary dividend proposed for FY2018 (interim 1.50 paid 22 Feb 2019).",
  "2018/2019 BS 'Investment property' line (76.9 / 78.0) placed in bs_other; it is included in total non-current assets. Same for 2020 (73.3) and 2021 (9; most reclassified to PP&E in Q4 2021 after the Group took over the lease to operate a store).",
  "2019 (2019 URD p.298-301): first year of IFRS 16, applied FULL RETROSPECTIVELY (IAS 8) with 2018 comparatives and 1 Jan 2018 opening balance restated; first-time application reduced 1 Jan 2018 equity by 34.3. New lines: right-of-use assets, lease liabilities (current / non-current), 'Repayment of lease liabilities' in financing cash flows, ROU amortisation and lease interest in net financial income.",
  "2019 memo.da_rou = 211.6 (Note 7 text: total ROU amortisation in opex incl. cost of sales); cash flow statement line shows 211.5 and Other income & expenses line shows 209.4; Note 14 ROU 'amortisation and impairment' = 218.2. memo.da_fixed = 236.2 (total fixed-asset D&A in opex incl. cost of sales; 197.5 within Other income & expenses).",
  "From 2019 the cash flow statement splits depreciation into three lines (fixed assets, right-of-use assets, impairment). cf.da / memo.da_cf hold the fixed-asset D&A line only (2019 236.2; 2020 271.0; 2021 312); ROU and impairment lines are in cf_other and memo. Sum of the three lines: 2019 476.2, 2020 568.5, 2021 628.",
  "2019 adjusted free cash flow introduced (= operating cash flows + change in WCR - operating investments - repayment of lease liabilities); 2019 URD Note 3 p.314.",
  "2019 dps = 5.00: ordinary dividend PROPOSED in the 2019 URD/Feb-2020 press release. Due to Covid-19 the Supervisory Board reduced it to 4.55 (approved at AGM 24 Apr 2020; 2020 URD Note 23.1).",
  "2019 restated net cash = net cash + cash investments >3 months (no deduction of financial liabilities). From 2020 the definition also deducts borrowings and financial liabilities (2020: -8.3); 2019 financial liabilities were 8.9 (not deducted).",
  "2020 non-recurring item: +91.1 = income from the deconsolidation of Shang Xia (Exor reserved capital increase, 23 Dec 2020), 2020 URD Note 2 & 8; booked in Holding segment; non-taxable. 2020 also includes acquisition of 100% of J3L (metal parts supplier, previously 30% associate) - 'Acquisitions of consolidated shares' -71.6.",
  "2020 Other income and expenses include a EUR 20m donation to AP-HP (EUR 7m in 2021).",
  "2020 and 2019 current lease liabilities both printed as 195.6 in the 2020 URD balance sheet and Note 14.2 (copied as printed).",
  "2020 restated net cash 4,903.5 reconciliation: net cash 4,716.9 (incl. +0.6 restatement of mark-to-market on liquidities) + 195.0 cash investments >3 months - 8.3 financial liabilities.",
  "2021 URD reports in whole EUR millions (rounded), so several subtotals differ by +-1 from the sum of components (e.g. sector sum 8,981 vs 8,982; geo sum 8,983; investing CF components sum -668 vs -669). Printed values kept.",
  "2021 constant-currency and current-rate growth rates taken from the FY2021 results press release (18 Feb 2022) which prints one decimal; the 2021 URD only prints whole percentages (e.g. 42%/41%). roi_margin 2021 = 39.3% from the press release (URD prints 39%).",
  "2021 segment 'Unallocated' (-50) replaces 'Holding': since 2021 it includes free share plan expenses and unallocated central costs and internal billings (previously allocated differently), so 2021 roi_unalloc and area ROI are not comparable with 2020 Holding (-208).",
  "2021: IFRIC April 2021 decision on IAS 19 (benefits attribution) applied; reduction of commitment of EUR 45m posted to equity (EUR 34m net of deferred tax) at 1 Jan 2021 (2021 URD Note 1.2). 2021 Perfumes renamed 'Perfume and Beauty' (Beauty launched 2020).",
